[[:db/retract 17592186194189 :answer-field/choices 17592186194192] [:db/retract 17592186194189 :answer-field/choices 17592186194193] [:db/retract 17592186194189 :answer-field/choices 17592186194194] [:db/retract 17592186194189 :answer-field/choices 17592186194190] [:db/retract 17592186194189 :answer-field/choices 17592186194191] {:db/id 17592186198389 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ef91d27f-5ce3-5c48-b5b9-4ec732b3b2e1" "question-92e8ddd2-ccb6-5c20-b74b-2f784e857a55" "question-29805411-7a4c-51f7-893d-a0f3dc3cef10"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198031 :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=\\left\\langle z+2y, \\: 3y+z, \\: x -z\\right\\rangle$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=-3x+2y$ for $0 \\leq x \\leq 2$ and $0 \\leq y \\leq 1.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $\\mathbf F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n![](images/c6/c682f99e66e12fb124beaee9ae090978444e402b74ce675f0eb2f7939c1ed06d.svg)\nWhat is the missing expression?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198392 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5b08ff1d-1edf-523c-a8e8-287f135b6040" "question-431ed508-ca53-50c3-b7a4-875fc9b23084"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ef91d27f-5ce3-5c48-b5b9-4ec732b3b2e1" :question/id #uuid "ef91d27f-5ce3-5c48-b5b9-4ec732b3b2e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-161471" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨x+z,\\,2z,\\,y+z⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=x-3y$ for $-1\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 3.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u-3v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,3,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x+z,\\,2z,\\,y+z⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=u-3v} \\\\  & =⟨u+u-3v,\\,2(u-3v),\\,v+u-3v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u-3v,\\,2u-6v,\\,u-2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨2u-3v,\\,2u-6v,\\,u-2v⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,3,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(2u-3v)\\cdot (-1)+(2u-6v)\\cdot (3)+(u-2v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2u+3v+6u-18v+u-2v \\\\  & =5u-17v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z-y,\\,2y-z,\\,xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5u-17v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}(5u-17v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-de6e4169-2fd0-5a0b-b7fe-172964aca58f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-de6e4169-2fd0-5a0b-b7fe-172964aca58f" :answer-field/id #uuid "de6e4169-2fd0-5a0b-b7fe-172964aca58f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9d9623af-3bba-5a0d-9c01-61a215703653" :answer-field/choices ["answer-86aaa33f-073f-5b9c-b6ed-02e42f1370d2" "answer-9d9623af-3bba-5a0d-9c01-61a215703653" "answer-8fa80cac-9ed0-54f2-a0fb-a71697486081" "answer-556660a7-ba40-5142-a23c-96cdb3bb38b3" "answer-b721d1da-8cb3-5423-bdff-f515271a77db"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86aaa33f-073f-5b9c-b6ed-02e42f1370d2" :answer/id #uuid "86aaa33f-073f-5b9c-b6ed-02e42f1370d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12u-v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d9623af-3bba-5a0d-9c01-61a215703653" :answer/id #uuid "9d9623af-3bba-5a0d-9c01-61a215703653" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5u-17v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8fa80cac-9ed0-54f2-a0fb-a71697486081" :answer/id #uuid "8fa80cac-9ed0-54f2-a0fb-a71697486081" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8u+14v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-556660a7-ba40-5142-a23c-96cdb3bb38b3" :answer/id #uuid "556660a7-ba40-5142-a23c-96cdb3bb38b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8u-23v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b721d1da-8cb3-5423-bdff-f515271a77db" :answer/id #uuid "b721d1da-8cb3-5423-bdff-f515271a77db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u-6v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198593 :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z-y,\\,2y-z,\\,xy⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=x+y$ for $0\\le x\\le 4$ and $-2\\le y\\le 3.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u+v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 4,\\,-2\\le v\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z-y,\\,2y-z,\\,xy⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=u+v} \\\\  & =⟨u+v-v,\\,2v-(u+v),\\,uv⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u,\\,v-u,\\,uv⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u,\\,v-u,\\,uv⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =u\\cdot (-1)+(v-u)\\cdot (-1)+uv\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-u-v+u+uv \\\\  & =uv-v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z-y,\\,2y-z,\\,xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(uv-v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{-2}^{3}uv-v\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186194189 :answer-field/correct "answer-63293960-e3b1-529e-96e9-642aedf596e5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cb8fdbef-d72d-513a-8e44-4a96d82e4382" "answer-e83e93b0-2e8f-5324-b1ed-23d683ac8523" "answer-1cea6d00-8d2b-5733-8616-9267687fd149" "answer-63293960-e3b1-529e-96e9-642aedf596e5" "answer-84b21f44-ef97-5299-8654-bb5534b15960"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb8fdbef-d72d-513a-8e44-4a96d82e4382" :answer/id #uuid "cb8fdbef-d72d-513a-8e44-4a96d82e4382" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{u}^{2}v-uv+{v}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e83e93b0-2e8f-5324-b1ed-23d683ac8523" :answer/id #uuid "e83e93b0-2e8f-5324-b1ed-23d683ac8523" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u+v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1cea6d00-8d2b-5733-8616-9267687fd149" :answer/id #uuid "1cea6d00-8d2b-5733-8616-9267687fd149" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "uv+v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-63293960-e3b1-529e-96e9-642aedf596e5" :answer/id #uuid "63293960-e3b1-529e-96e9-642aedf596e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "uv-v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84b21f44-ef97-5299-8654-bb5534b15960" :answer/id #uuid "84b21f44-ef97-5299-8654-bb5534b15960" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{2}+uv+{v}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-92e8ddd2-ccb6-5c20-b74b-2f784e857a55" :question/id #uuid "92e8ddd2-ccb6-5c20-b74b-2f784e857a55" :question/math-academy-id "q-161379" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨(x+y)^{2},\\,(x-y)^{2},\\,xy⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=y-x$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $-3\\le y\\le 0.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-3}^{0}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,v-u⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,-3\\le v\\le 0\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨(x+y)^{2},\\,(x-y)^{2},\\,xy⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=v-u} \\\\  & =⟨(u+v)^{2},\\,(u-v)^{2},\\,uv⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨(u+v)^{2},\\,(u-v)^{2},\\,uv⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(u+v)^{2}\\cdot 1+(u-v)^{2}\\cdot (-1)+uv\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =5uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨(x+y)^{2},\\,(x-y)^{2},\\,xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5uv)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-3}^{0}5uv\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dce1231b-682c-5119-8b60-1e600b81511c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dce1231b-682c-5119-8b60-1e600b81511c" :answer-field/id #uuid "dce1231b-682c-5119-8b60-1e600b81511c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-57bc1e11-c92f-5bf5-b1cd-bdfca274f1c3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0b89c0b5-bd8b-5088-a053-0db9bc0fd31f" "answer-62a07ee3-0b12-5f4d-81e0-7183964e0136" "answer-57bc1e11-c92f-5bf5-b1cd-bdfca274f1c3" "answer-876d48e1-3fb3-5bc6-88d3-a7e99ab5d29a" "answer-b65ee624-a7db-5060-ba14-007644627aeb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b89c0b5-bd8b-5088-a053-0db9bc0fd31f" :answer/id #uuid "0b89c0b5-bd8b-5088-a053-0db9bc0fd31f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-uv" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62a07ee3-0b12-5f4d-81e0-7183964e0136" :answer/id #uuid "62a07ee3-0b12-5f4d-81e0-7183964e0136" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3u{v}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57bc1e11-c92f-5bf5-b1cd-bdfca274f1c3" :answer/id #uuid "57bc1e11-c92f-5bf5-b1cd-bdfca274f1c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5uv" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-876d48e1-3fb3-5bc6-88d3-a7e99ab5d29a" :answer/id #uuid "876d48e1-3fb3-5bc6-88d3-a7e99ab5d29a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "uv+v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b65ee624-a7db-5060-ba14-007644627aeb" :answer/id #uuid "b65ee624-a7db-5060-ba14-007644627aeb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "uv-v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-29805411-7a4c-51f7-893d-a0f3dc3cef10" :question/id #uuid "29805411-7a4c-51f7-893d-a0f3dc3cef10" :question/math-academy-id "q-161377" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨{x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,{y}^{2}-{z}^{2},\\,{z}^{2}⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=-x-y$ for $-2\\le x\\le 2$ and $-2\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,-u-v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 2,\\,-2\\le v\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨{x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,{y}^{2}-{z}^{2},\\,{z}^{2}⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=-u-v} \\\\  & =⟨{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,{v}^{2}-(-u-v)^{2},\\,(-u-v)^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,{v}^{2}-(-u-v)^{2},\\,(-u-v)^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\cdot (1)+({v}^{2}-(-u-v)^{2})\\cdot (1)+(-u-v)^{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={u}^{2}-{v}^{2}+{v}^{2}-(-u-v)^{2}+(-u-v)^{2} \\\\  & ={u}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨{x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,{y}^{2}-{z}^{2},\\,{z}^{2}⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2bbc92cc-19ad-54ee-9d42-9ce995a00f4a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2bbc92cc-19ad-54ee-9d42-9ce995a00f4a" :answer-field/id #uuid "2bbc92cc-19ad-54ee-9d42-9ce995a00f4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-146aebe7-02b6-58b6-8dd1-374b1fcd30d0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6197b42b-5e97-5e6b-a1bb-2951dc50be38" "answer-cacced8e-053e-5057-89f0-678a72c14a18" "answer-3586c1bc-3061-5093-99ca-95e798991986" "answer-146aebe7-02b6-58b6-8dd1-374b1fcd30d0" "answer-5a1a3ab5-07e2-55d2-b713-d20c37bdda9e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6197b42b-5e97-5e6b-a1bb-2951dc50be38" :answer/id #uuid "6197b42b-5e97-5e6b-a1bb-2951dc50be38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2uv" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cacced8e-053e-5057-89f0-678a72c14a18" :answer/id #uuid "cacced8e-053e-5057-89f0-678a72c14a18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3v" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3586c1bc-3061-5093-99ca-95e798991986" :answer/id #uuid "3586c1bc-3061-5093-99ca-95e798991986" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4uv" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-146aebe7-02b6-58b6-8dd1-374b1fcd30d0" :answer/id #uuid "146aebe7-02b6-58b6-8dd1-374b1fcd30d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a1a3ab5-07e2-55d2-b713-d20c37bdda9e" :answer/id #uuid "5a1a3ab5-07e2-55d2-b713-d20c37bdda9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186373986 :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,4u-v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,\\,1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨2x-z,\\,y-z,\\,z+y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=4u-v} \\\\  & =⟨2u-(4u-v),\\,v-(4u-v),\\,4u-v+v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2u+v,\\,-4u+2v,\\,4u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨-2u+v,\\,-4u+2v,\\,4u⟩\\cdot ⟨-4,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(-2u+v)\\cdot (-4)+(-4u+2v)\\cdot 1+4u\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =8u-4v+-4u+2v+4u \\\\  & =8u-2v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨2x-z,\\,y-z,\\,z+y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(8u-2v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(8u-2v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-5b08ff1d-1edf-523c-a8e8-287f135b6040" :question/id #uuid "5b08ff1d-1edf-523c-a8e8-287f135b6040" :question/math-academy-id "q-162607" :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}-Q\\frac{\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}{∂y}+\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $z=g(x,y),$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=⟨x,\\,y,\\,g(x,y)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂x}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂y}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & \\frac{∂g}{∂x} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\end{aligned}|=⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,y))\\cdot ({r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2a3936a3-b7fb-5980-bcc0-5a21e600fc1e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2a3936a3-b7fb-5980-bcc0-5a21e600fc1e" :answer-field/id #uuid "2a3936a3-b7fb-5980-bcc0-5a21e600fc1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f2a31230-1787-5f1a-a9cf-ba9794a07b89" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f0b4e080-429e-59c9-b7b0-c3e775d0e61a" "answer-73c7f141-a638-5c2f-a226-4db1e183214c" "answer-d23fc8da-8bb8-570e-94f8-2dd437e7348c" "answer-f2a31230-1787-5f1a-a9cf-ba9794a07b89" "answer-45ff11c7-5335-5ffb-9240-826266b3b1ec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0b4e080-429e-59c9-b7b0-c3e775d0e61a" :answer/id #uuid "f0b4e080-429e-59c9-b7b0-c3e775d0e61a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$∂x,∂g,$ and $-1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73c7f141-a638-5c2f-a226-4db1e183214c" :answer/id #uuid "73c7f141-a638-5c2f-a226-4db1e183214c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$∂x,∂g,$ and $-R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d23fc8da-8bb8-570e-94f8-2dd437e7348c" :answer/id #uuid "d23fc8da-8bb8-570e-94f8-2dd437e7348c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$∂x,∂g,$ and $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2a31230-1787-5f1a-a9cf-ba9794a07b89" :answer/id #uuid "f2a31230-1787-5f1a-a9cf-ba9794a07b89" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$∂x,∂g,$ and $R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45ff11c7-5335-5ffb-9240-826266b3b1ec" :answer/id #uuid "45ff11c7-5335-5ffb-9240-826266b3b1ec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$∂z,∂g,$ and $-1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-431ed508-ca53-50c3-b7a4-875fc9b23084" :question/id #uuid "431ed508-ca53-50c3-b7a4-875fc9b23084" :question/math-academy-id "q-161449" :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $z={x}^{2}y$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\,xy+\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\,{x}^{2}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $z={x}^{2}y,$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=⟨x,\\,y,\\,{x}^{2}y⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2xy⟩ \\\\ {r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,{x}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2xy \\\\ 0 & 1 & {x}^{2}\\end{aligned}|=⟨-2xy,\\,-{x}^{2},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,y))\\cdot ({r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨-2xy,\\,-{x}^{2},\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-2P\\,xy+(\\,-Q\\,)\\,{x}^{2}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b4de48c6-077d-5787-a098-9c9aedaea635"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b4de48c6-077d-5787-a098-9c9aedaea635" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4de48c6-077d-5787-a098-9c9aedaea635" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-92e3c6dc-2a2e-5a89-badd-5c261850de58" :answer-field/choices ["answer-92e3c6dc-2a2e-5a89-badd-5c261850de58" "answer-f0f8eac7-f04f-5d8d-a984-6504f0ab8abc" "answer-65b0d9ca-824a-5dcc-9c38-6fd9b637f302" "answer-c4841ceb-b2a6-58c8-96a9-bc8ce5fca6d0" "answer-f233c1ca-3c84-5c07-9f36-b49ccdff39a8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92e3c6dc-2a2e-5a89-badd-5c261850de58" :answer/id #uuid "92e3c6dc-2a2e-5a89-badd-5c261850de58" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-2P$ and $-Q$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0f8eac7-f04f-5d8d-a984-6504f0ab8abc" :answer/id #uuid "f0f8eac7-f04f-5d8d-a984-6504f0ab8abc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-2R$ and $Q$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65b0d9ca-824a-5dcc-9c38-6fd9b637f302" :answer/id #uuid "65b0d9ca-824a-5dcc-9c38-6fd9b637f302" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-4P$ and $-2Q$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4841ceb-b2a6-58c8-96a9-bc8ce5fca6d0" :answer/id #uuid "c4841ceb-b2a6-58c8-96a9-bc8ce5fca6d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-4Q$ and $P$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f233c1ca-3c84-5c07-9f36-b49ccdff39a8" :answer/id #uuid "f233c1ca-3c84-5c07-9f36-b49ccdff39a8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ and $-R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186278519 :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $x=k(y,z)$ for $(y,z)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(P-\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\,\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}-R\\,\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186401247 :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}{∂x}-\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\frac{∂g}{\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186401240 :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $y=2x{z}^{3}$ for $(x,z)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\,{z}^{3}+Q-\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\,x{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?\n\n*Hint: The orientation of $S$ should be chosen such that the unit normal vector has a positive  $j$-component.*" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186199473 :tutorial/content "Let's calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=\\left\\langle (x-y)^2, \\:(x+y)^2, \\: 12xy \\right\\rangle\n$$\n\n \n\nthrough the surface $S$ defined by the Cartesian equation \n\n$$\nz=2y-2x\n$$\n\nfor $0 \\leq x \\leq 1$ and $0 \\leq y \\leq 1.$ \n\nFor surfaces like this, substituting $x=u$ and $y=v,$ we obtain a parametrization \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle u,\\: v,\\: 2v-2u \\right\\rangle\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (u,v) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq u \\leq 1, \\: 0 \\leq v \\leq 1 \\big\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nRecall that for a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n} \\,\\textrm{d}S\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\cdot (\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v) \\,\\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2v-2u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2v-2u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,-2,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨(x-y)^{2},\\,(x+y)^{2},\\,12xy⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=2v-2u} \\\\  & =⟨(u-v)^{2},\\,(u+v)^{2},\\,12uv⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and $\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨(u-v)^{2},\\,(u+v)^{2},\\,12uv⟩\\cdot ⟨2,\\,-2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(u-v)^{2}\\cdot 2+(u+v)^{2}\\cdot (-2)+12uv\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux of $\\mathbf F$ through $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨(x-y)^{2},\\,(x+y)^{2},\\,12xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}4uv\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}4uv\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2u\\,\\text{d}u\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}2v\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =[{u}^{2}]_{0}^{1}\\cdot [{v}^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =({1}^{2}-{0}^{2})\\cdot ({1}^{2}-{0}^{2}) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186199470 :tutorial/content "Let's now derive a general formula for the flux through an *upward-oriented* Cartesian surface.\n\nFor a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n} \\,\\textrm{d}S\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\cdot (\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v) \\,\\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nConsider a surface $S$ given by the equation $z=g(x,y).$ The canonical parameterization of the surface is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(x,y) = \\left\\langle x,\\: y,\\: g(x,y) \\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nComputing the tangent vectors to the grid curves, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂x}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂y}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & \\frac{∂g}{∂x} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\end{aligned}|=⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the $\\mathbf k$-component is positive, which indicates that our surface is upward-oriented.\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,y))\\cdot ({r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize as follows:\n\n- *For a surface $S$ given by $z = g(x,y)$ for $(x,y) \\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) = \\left\\langle P,\\: Q,\\: R \\right\\rangle$ over $S$ is given by*\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\left( -P\\dfrac{\\partial g}{\\partial x} - Q\\dfrac{\\partial g}{\\partial y} + R \\right) \\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe have analogous results for surfaces of the form $y = h(x,z)$ and $x=k(y,z){:}$\n\n- *For a surface $S$ given by $y = h(x,z)$ for $(x,z) \\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) = \\left\\langle P,\\: Q,\\: R \\right\\rangle$ over $S$ is given by*\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\left( -P\\dfrac{\\partial h}{\\partial x} + Q - R\\dfrac{\\partial h}{\\partial z} \\right) \\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\n*where the unit normal to the surface is chosen such that the $\\mathbf j$-component is positive.*\n\n- *For a surface $S$ given $x = k(y,z)$ for $(y,z) \\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) = \\left\\langle P,\\: Q,\\: R \\right\\rangle$ over $S$ is given by*\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\left( P - Q\\dfrac{\\partial k}{\\partial y} - R\\dfrac{\\partial k}{\\partial z} \\right) \\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\n*where the unit normal to the surface is chosen such that the $\\mathbf i$-component is positive.*" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198485 :activity/expected-seconds 1020.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
